[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Class 6 Single Segment Medium Risk Security Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @vcr_grammar

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document specifies cybersecurity requirements for Class 6 vehicle components: **Single Segment Medium Risk**.

Class 6 devices are truck modules connected to a single vehicle network segment found to have a medium overall fleet risk.

Examples include:
- Suspension - Steer Axle / ECS / ECAS (J1939 SA 20)
- Suspension - System Controller #1 (J1939 SA 47)
- Automated Driving (L0-L2) / Forward Looking Camera / Radar (Bendix FLR/FLC)
- Engine Valve Controller (J1939 SA 00)
- Clutch/Converter Unit (J1939 SA 78)
- Auxiliary Transmission (J1939 SA 16)
- Collision Avoidance (J1939 SA 42)
- Body Controller (Key-Lock Options)
- Shift Console Primary / Gearshift ECU (J1939 SA 05)
- Safety Restraint System / SRS (J1939 SA 83)
- Vehicle Dynamic Stability Controller (J1939 SA 62)
- Pyrometer
- Adaptive Front Lighting System (J1939 SA 71)
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Baseline Security Requirements Applicability

